{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-95c10aa6-da02-43db-9f95-3e9dba0902da","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc22375c204fe7ba","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9019-w1fjql68/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9019-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9019 (Curated getting-started tutorial gallery)\n\n## Triage Outcome\n\nNot below-threshold and not docs-only. The strategy explicitly spans three\narchitecturally distinct work streams with different owners and review\nprocesses — product code (Dashboard gallery and launch mechanics), substantive\ncontent authoring (the six curated tutorials), and documentation — across four\ncomponents (Dashboard, Notebooks, Data Science Pipelines, Documentation).\nThe multiple-distinct-work-streams escape condition applies, so the strategy\nproceeds to full decomposition.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Tutorial packaging format and validation manifest | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Dashboard tutorial gallery and launch mechanics | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Author five notebook-based getting-started tutorials | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Author the first-pipeline getting-started tutorial | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Document tutorial gallery usage and contribution process | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 Tutorial packaging format\"] --> E002[\"E002 Dashboard gallery\"]\n    E001 --> E003[\"E003 Notebook tutorials\"]\n    E001 --> E004[\"E004 Pipeline tutorial\"]\n    E001 --> E005[\"E005 Documentation\"]\n    E002 --> E005\n    E003 --> E005\n    E004 --> E005\n```\n\nArrows point from dependency to dependent (E001 must complete before E002 can\nstart).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E002 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | The gallery's launch mechanics build against the tutorial packaging format: they parse tutorial metadata and pinned images to open a workbench with the notebook or import the pipeline. The format is a build-against artifact (an API-like contract), not a configuration reference, so the edge is serial. |\n| E001 → E003 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The notebook tutorials are packaged per the format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) so they are versioned and testable; content is built against the contract. |\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | Same as above for the pipeline tutorial, whose package must carry the metadata and validation manifest the format defines. |\n| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs blocked by all Implementations) | Documentation must describe the packaging/versioning model that was actually defined. |\n| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 | Docs describe the gallery that was built. |\n| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 | Docs describe the tutorial set and (per HLR-4) the contribution process the tutorial packaging implies. |\n| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 | Same — the pipeline tutorial is part of the documented tutorial set. |\n\n**Parallel non-edges (deliberate):**\n\n- **E002 ∥ E003 ∥ E004** — the gallery, the notebook tutorials, and the\n  pipeline tutorial run in parallel once the format is defined. The gallery\n  consumes the *format*, not specific tutorial content: its acceptance\n  criterion is verified with any format-conformant tutorial package, so there\n  is no artifact dependency on the content epics. Serializing gallery behind\n  content (or vice versa) would fabricate a dependency the strategy does not\n  have — HLR-3 exists precisely so tutorials are versioned and testable\n  independently of Dashboard releases.\n- No `konflux-onboarding`, `repo-onboarding`, or `license-validation` epics:\n  Dashboard, Notebooks, and Data Science Pipelines are all existing,\n  Konflux-onboarded components per architecture context, so Rule 20/25 do not\n  apply and no \"build pipeline green\" DAG coupling exists.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|-----|----------|------------------------|---------|-------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | Dashboard tutorial gallery with one-click launch into the user's project (workbench with notebook, or pipeline import) | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Direct map. Launch mechanics consume the packaging format defined upstream. |\n| HLR-2 | P0 | Six curated tutorials covering the core journeys, each tested against the current release | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Split by component/team boundary (Rule 1): five notebook-journey tutorials → Notebooks/Workbenches; the first-pipeline tutorial → Data Science Pipelines/RHOAI Pipelines. Both epics share HLR-2 and both are P0, so no priority bundling judgment is needed. |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) for versioned, independently testable tutorials | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Direct map. Strategy labels this P1, but E001 is elevated to P0 by priority inheritance: it is the shared contract every P0 epic (gallery, both tutorial epics) builds against, so it blocks all P0 work (Step 4: \"an epic blocking all P0 work is implicitly P0\"). |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers using the gallery and the contribution process | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Direct map. docs-authoring priority exception: strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1 (not P2), and the epic does not push priority upstream to the implementations it depends on. |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n  Teams table, no Dependencies table, no formal Given/When/Then Acceptance\n  Criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements section. Decomposition\n  proceeded with available information; owning teams were taken from\n  architecture context (`dashboard.md`, `notebooks.md`,\n  `data-science-pipelines.md`). Per-epic acceptance criteria were derived\n  from the HLRs.\n- **Team inference for Documentation**: the Documentation component has no\n  architecture-context file, so no owning team is on record; the epic is\n  assigned to a generic \"RHOAI Documentation\" team. Verify with the actual\n  docs team.\n- **Priority elevation of HLR-3** (observation, not an inversion): the\n  strategy marks the packaging format P1, but as the shared build-against\n  contract for all P0 work it is P0 by rule-mandated inheritance. If the\n  gallery could ship with an ad-hoc tutorial list and the format formalized\n  later, the strategy author's P1 intent would conflict with the\n  shared-surface rule (two epics building the same metadata structure\n  independently); the inheritance path was chosen to avoid that boundary\n  violation.\n- **Epic-size overage on E003** (managed): authoring and testing five\n  notebook tutorials may exceed the ~2-week epic guideline. Kept intact per\n  the one-logical-change rule: HLR-2 presents the tutorial set as a single\n  work item — one curation standard applied uniformly to an enumerated set\n  of journeys, sharing the packaging format, review criteria, and test\n  machinery; splitting forces duplicate setup and fragments one logical\n  change. **Conditional re-split trigger:** if validated authoring effort per\n  tutorial materially exceeds the plan (e.g., any single tutorial requires\n  more than a quarter of the epic's budget), or capacity constraints require\n  independently schedulable units, re-split E003 by journey cluster (e.g.,\n  workbench/data-prep vs. training/deployment/RAG).\n- **Scope-trap check** (clean): the out-of-scope list (no community\n  contribution tooling, no localization) is consistent with HLR-4, which\n  requires only that the contribution *process* be *documented*. The\n  documentation epic's scope explicitly excludes submission tooling.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — the strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain\ntiming (its dependency table is absent and no upstream/vendor coordination\nappears in the text), so there is no Tier 1/Tier 2 split. The internal\nparallelism (gallery ∥ tutorials after the format) already provides\nincremental delivery.\n\n## Component Mapping Notes\n\nCanonical component names are used verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`.\nTwo non-obvious mappings:\n\n- **E001 (packaging format) → `Dashboard`**: the format spans Dashboard\n  (consuming launch mechanics), Notebooks, and Data Science Pipelines (content\n  packaging). Assigned the single most-relevant canonical name — Dashboard,\n  the component whose code parses the contract — with the span noted here.\n- **Tutorial content → `Notebooks` / `Data Science Pipelines`**: the six\n  tutorials are content, not code changes to those components; the notebook\n  medium maps to Notebooks (Workbenches team) and the pipeline tutorial to\n  Data Science Pipelines (RHOAI Pipelines team), matching the affected\n  components list.\n- **E005 → `Documentation`**: canonical name exists in the list; no\n  architecture-context file backs it (reflected in that epic's\n  architecture_claims signal).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33167,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8204eaf88c5b320b","agent_id":"a773be1ca309a3bac","session_id":"59336e95-0b73-4918-bc9d-0677bfcc1dda","uuid":"c02deb2c-d129-4c88-9294-154aee77853d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:24:41.803Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019"}
