mage references, and validation manifest, such that a third party can\n  package a tutorial without further guidance.\n- A tutorial packaged per the format can be versioned and re-tested without\n  a Dashboard release (a version bump of a tutorial package does not require\n  any Dashboard change).\n- The validation mechanism, run against the worked example package, produces\n  a deterministic pass result; run against a deliberately broken package, it\n  produces a deterministic fail result identifying the violated manifest\n  entries.\n- The specification is reviewed and accepted by the teams implementing the\n  gallery and authoring the tutorials, with the acceptance recorded.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)** — tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images,\n  validation manifest) defined so tutorials are versioned and testable\n  independently of Dashboard releases. This epic covers HLR-3 in full.\n  Note: this epic is scheduled at P0 (not the HLR's stated P1) because it is\n  the shared contract that all P0 work in this strategy builds against —\n  priority inheritance applies.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36077,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8204eaf88c5b320b","agent_id":"a773be1ca309a3bac","session_id":"59336e95-0b73-4918-bc9d-0677bfcc1dda","uuid":"894f19db-663b-4d21-b727-65592e9bb606","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:24:58.225Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019"}
