{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a26d867e59a9d689","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9019 (Curated getting-started tutorial gallery)\n11\t\n12\t## Triage Outcome\n13\t\n14\tNot below-threshold and not docs-only. The strategy explicitly spans three\n15\tarchitecturally distinct work streams with different owners and review\n16\tprocesses — product code (Dashboard gallery and launch mechanics), substantive\n17\tcontent authoring (the six curated tutorials), and documentation — across four\n18\tcomponents (Dashboard, Notebooks, Data Science Pipelines, Documentation).\n19\tThe multiple-distinct-work-streams escape condition applies, so the strategy\n20\tproceeds to full decomposition.\n21\t\n22\t## Epic List\n23\t\n24\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n25\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Tutorial packaging format and validation manifest | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Dashboard tutorial gallery and launch mechanics | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Author five notebook-based getting-started tutorials | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Author the first-pipeline getting-started tutorial | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Document tutorial gallery usage and contribution process | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n31\t\n32\t## Dependency DAG\n33\t\n34\t```mermaid\n35\tgraph TD\n36\t    E001[\"E001 Tutorial packaging format\"] --> E002[\"E002 Dashboard gallery\"]\n37\t    E001 --> E003[\"E003 Notebook tutorials\"]\n38\t    E001 --> E004[\"E004 Pipeline tutorial\"]\n39\t    E001 --> E005[\"E005 Documentation\"]\n40\t    E002 --> E005\n41\t    E003 --> E005\n42\t    E004 --> E005\n43\t```\n44\t\n45\tArrows point from dependency to dependent (E001 must complete before E002 can\n46\tstart).\n47\t\n48\t## DAG Justification\n49\t\n50\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n51\t|------|------|-----------|\n52\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | The gallery's launch mechanics build against the tutorial packaging format: they parse tutorial metadata and pinned images to open a workbench with the notebook or import the pipeline. The format is a build-against artifact (an API-like contract), not a configuration reference, so the edge is serial. |\n53\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The notebook tutorials are packaged per the format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) so they are versioned and testable; content is built against the contract. |\n54\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | Same as above for the pipeline tutorial, whose package must carry the metadata and validation manifest the format defines. |\n55\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs blocked by all Implementations) | Documentation must describe the packaging/versioning model that was actually defined. |\n56\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 | Docs describe the gallery that was built. |\n57\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 | Docs describe the tutorial set and (per HLR-4) the contribution process the tutorial packaging implies. |\n58\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 | Same — the pipeline tutorial is part of the documented tutorial set. |\n59\t\n60\t**Parallel non-edges (deliberate):**\n61\t\n62\t- **E002 ∥ E003 ∥ E004** — the gallery, the notebook tutorials, and the\n63\t  pipeline tutorial run in parallel once the format is defined. The gallery\n64\t  consumes the *format*, not specific tutorial content: its acceptance\n65\t  criterion is verified with any format-conformant tutorial package, so there\n66\t  is no artifact dependency on the content epics. Serializing gallery behind\n67\t  content (or vice versa) would fabricate a dependency the strategy does not\n68\t  have — HLR-3 exists precisely so tutorials are versioned and testable\n69\t  independently of Dashboard releases.\n70\t- No `konflux-onboarding`, `repo-onboarding`, or `license-validation` epics:\n71\t  Dashboard, Notebooks, and Data Science Pipelines are all existing,\n72\t  Konflux-onboarded components per architecture context, so Rule 20/25 do not\n73\t  apply and no \"build pipeline green\" DAG coupling exists.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n76\t\n77\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epic(s) | Notes |\n78\t|-----|----------|------------------------|---------|-------|\n79\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Dashboard tutorial gallery with one-click launch into the user's project (workbench with notebook, or pipeline import) | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Direct map. Launch mechanics consume the packaging format defined upstream. |\n80\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Six curated tutorials covering the core journeys, each tested against the current release | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Split by component/team boundary (Rule 1): five notebook-journey tutorials → Notebooks/Workbenches; the first-pipeline tutorial → Data Science Pipelines/RHOAI Pipelines. Both epics share HLR-2 and both are P0, so no priority bundling judgment is needed. |\n81\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) for versioned, independently testable tutorials | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Direct map. Strategy labels this P1, but E001 is elevated to P0 by priority inheritance: it is the shared contract every P0 epic (gallery, both tutorial epics) builds against, so it blocks all P0 work (Step 4: \"an epic blocking all P0 work is implicitly P0\"). |\n82\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers using the gallery and the contribution process | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Direct map. docs-authoring priority exception: strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1 (not P2), and the epic does not push priority upstream to the implementations it depends on. |\n83\t\n84\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n85\t\n86\t## Health Warnings\n87\t\n88\t- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n89\t  Teams table, no Dependencies table, no formal Given/When/Then Acceptance\n90\t  Criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements section. Decomposition\n91\t  proceeded with available information; owning teams were taken from\n92\t  architecture context (`dashboard.md`, `notebooks.md`,\n93\t  `data-science-pipelines.md`). Per-epic acceptance criteria were derived\n94\t  from the HLRs.\n95\t- **Team inference for Documentation**: the Documentation component has no\n96\t  architecture-context file, so no owning team is on record; the epic is\n97\t  assigned to a generic \"RHOAI Documentation\" team. Verify with the actual\n98\t  docs team.\n99\t- **Priority elevation of HLR-3** (observation, not an inversion): the\n100\t  strategy marks the packaging format P1, but as the shared build-against\n101\t  contract for all P0 work it is P0 by rule-mandated inheritance. If the\n102\t  gallery could ship with an ad-hoc tutorial list and the format formalized\n103\t  later, the strategy author's P1 intent would conflict with the\n104\t  shared-surface rule (two epics building the same metadata structure\n105\t  independently); the inheritance path was chosen to avoid that boundary\n106\t  violation.\n107\t- **Epic-size overage on E003** (managed): authoring and testing five\n108\t  notebook tutorials may exceed the ~2-week epic guideline. Kept intact per\n109\t  the one-logical-change rule: HLR-2 presents the tutorial set as a single\n110\t  work item — one curation standard applied uniformly to an enumerated set\n111\t  of journeys, sharing the packaging format, review criteria, and test\n112\t  machinery; splitting forces duplicate setup and fragments one logical\n113\t  change. **Conditional re-split trigger:** if validated authoring effort per\n114\t  tutorial materially exceeds the plan (e.g., any single tutorial requires\n115\t  more than a quarter of the epic's budget), or capacity constraints require\n116\t  independently schedulable units, re-split E003 by journey cluster (e.g.,\n117\t  workbench/data-prep vs. training/deployment/RAG).\n118\t- **Scope-trap check** (clean): the out-of-scope list (no community\n119\t  contribution tooling, no localization) is consistent with HLR-4, which\n120\t  requires only that the contribution *process* be *documented*. The\n121\t  documentation epic's scope explicitly excludes submission tooling.\n122\t\n123\t## Tiered Delivery\n124\t\n125\tNot applicable — the strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain\n126\ttiming (its dependency table is absent and no upstream/vendor coordination\n127\tappears in the text), so there is no Tier 1/Tier 2 split. The internal\n128\tparallelism (gallery ∥ tutorials after the format) already provides\n129\tincremental delivery.\n130\t\n131\t## Component Mapping Notes\n132\t\n133\tCanonical component names are used verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`.\n134\tTwo non-obvious mappings:\n135\t\n136\t- **E001 (packaging format) → `Dashboard`**: the format spans Dashboard\n137\t  (consuming launch mechanics), Notebooks, and Data Science Pipelines (content\n138\t  packaging). Assigned the single most-relevant canonical name — Dashboard,\n139\t  the component whose code parses the contract — with the span noted here.\n140\t- **Tutorial content → `Notebooks` / `Data Science Pipelines`**: the six\n141\t  tutorials are content, not code changes to those components; the notebook\n142\t  medium maps to Notebooks (Workbenches team) and the pipeline tutorial to\n143\t  Data Science Pipelines (RHOAI Pipelines team), matching the affected\n144\t  components list.\n145\t- **E005 → `Documentation`**: canonical name exists in the list; no\n146\t  architecture-context file backs it (reflected in that epic's\n147\t  architectur