{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcbd2510aeacbd4e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9019-E001\n3\ttitle: Tutorial packaging format and validation manifest\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 0\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Tutorial packaging format and validation manifest\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic defines the tutorial packaging format: the contract that makes a\n34\ttutorial a versioned, independently testable artifact, decoupled from\n35\tDashboard releases. It specifies the tutorial package metadata, the pinned\n36\timage references a tutorial runs on, and the validation manifest used to test\n37\ta tutorial against a platform release, plus the validation mechanism that\n38\texecutes that manifest. This is the shared interface that the Dashboard\n39\ttutorial gallery's launch mechanics consume and that every curated tutorial\n40\tis packaged with.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Define the tutorial package structure: metadata identifying the tutorial\n45\t  (title, journey, description), the pinned workbench images it runs on, and\n46\t  pointers to the tutorial payload (notebook or pipeline definition).\n47\t- Define the validation manifest schema: the machine-checkable statement of\n48\t  what a tutorial must satisfy against a given platform release, so tutorial\n49\t  testing runs without a Dashboard release.\n50\t- Define the versioning model for tutorial packages so tutorials can be\n51\t  updated and re-tested independently of Dashboard release cadence.\n52\t- Provide the validation mechanism that checks a packaged tutorial against\n53\t  its manifest and reports a deterministic pass/fail result.\n54\t- Produce a worked example package demonstrating the format end to end.\n55\t- Review the format with the teams that build the gallery and author the\n56\t  tutorials, and record their acceptance.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- The format specification documents the package metadata fields, pinned\n61\t  image references, and validation manifest, such that a third party can\n62\t  package a tutorial without further guidance.\n63\t- A tutorial packaged per the format can be versioned and re-tested without\n64\t  a Dashboard release (a version bump of a tutorial package does not require\n65\t  any Dashboard change).\n66\t- The validation mechanism, run against the worked example package, produces\n67\t  a deterministic pass result; run against a deliberately broken package, it\n68\t  produces a deterministic fail result identifying the violated manifest\n69\t  entries.\n70\t- The specification is reviewed and accepted by the teams implementing the\n71\t  gallery and authoring the tutorials, with the acceptance recorded.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- **HLR-3 (P1)** — tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images,\n76\t  validation manifest) defined so tutorials are versioned and testable\n77\t  independently of Dashboard releases. This epic covers HLR-3 in full.\n78\t  Note: this epic is scheduled at P0 (not the HLR's stated P1) because it is\n79\t  the shared contract that all P0 work in this strategy builds against —\n80\t  priority inheritance applies.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e632fe8c4c11872","agent_id":"a8d916b83c342f671","session_id":"59336e95-0b73-4918-bc9d-0677bfcc1dda","uuid":"cb953b20-e820-48d